  <div class="bhd-page__split-copy">
    <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Claim progression</p>
    <h2>Marketing language should lag behind evidence, not lead it</h2>
    <p>The safest clinical-development convention is to separate four statements: what physiology suggests, what the product label authorizes, what a study is designed to test, and what completed results actually demonstrate.</p>
    <p>For example, an NPN supports sale under the authorized conditions of use. A future clinical protocol may investigate a more specific setting. Until that work is completed and interpreted appropriately, the protocol objective remains a question rather than a product benefit.</p>
  </div>
</section>

